# Model selections refreshed 2026-10-09 from job-hunt-kit-template commit 4582b18.
# https://github.com/jpita/job-hunt-kit-template/blob/4582b18/evals/BENCHMARKS.md
# Toolkit results are text-classification checks, not functional web-QA scores.
# Installed CLI versions observed 2026-10-09: Claude Code 2.1.289; Codex 0.160.0;
# Grok Build 1.0.46; Kimi Code 0.40.1; Reasonix 1.36.0; Antigravity 1.2.14;
# Copilot 1.0.93-1. These observations do not install or pin host binaries.
# Remaining provider pricing/availability notes below were researched 2026-10-02.
# Sourced by run-agent.sh and preflight.sh; this is shell syntax, not dotenv.
# Change a MODEL_* selection to an exact selector from its catalog below.
# Or override one invocation: MODEL_CODEX=gpt-6-astra bash scripts/run-agent.sh codex
# Catalogs do not run anything or configure providers. Provider-only entries need
# routing/account setup before selection. Availability is a dated observation.
# Tags describe intended positioning, NOT measured QA performance or equal tiers.
# cheap = economical within that provider; fast = speed-oriented;
# balanced = general tradeoff; frontier = high-capability positioning;
# reasoning, coding, vision, legacy, deprecated, restricted, auto are descriptive.
# API unit pricing is not the same as subscription quota or total task cost.

# Selected defaults: models exercised in the latest toolkit work, except Gemini
# (catalog-listed only). Reasoning settings may differ from those text-only evals.
MODEL_CLAUDE="${MODEL_CLAUDE:-claude-haiku-5-5}"
MODEL_CODEX="${MODEL_CODEX:-gpt-6-luna}"
MODEL_GROK="${MODEL_GROK:-grok-4.7}" # authenticated grok.com route; no separate API key
MODEL_KIMI="${MODEL_KIMI:-moonshotai/kimi-k3}"
MODEL_DEEPSEEK="${MODEL_DEEPSEEK:-deepseek-pro}" # alias -> deepseek-v4-pro
MODEL_ANTIGRAVITY="${MODEL_ANTIGRAVITY:-gemini-3.8-flash-low}"
ANTIGRAVITY_EFFORT="${ANTIGRAVITY_EFFORT:-low}" # match the selected Gemini effort variant
MODEL_COPILOT="${MODEL_COPILOT-}" # empty = account Auto; not a pinned model

# Row format: selector|comma-separated tags|availability|notes
# listed-local = CLI/account catalog, not an inference test.
# listed-api = authenticated provider /models response, not an inference test.
# documented = first-party supported ID; account access has not been tested.
# verified-run = historical model response, not proof of browser-QA readiness.
# verified-classification = answered in the toolkit text-classification eval.
# No hidden/internal Codex models, retired Claude models, or stale Kimi config IDs.

# CLAUDE CODE
# Sources: https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/overview
# https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/model-deprecations
# https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing
# https://code.claude.com/docs/en/model-config
# Local Fable option also appears in ~/.claude.json model-options cache.
# Prefer exact IDs below over moving CLI aliases best/fable/opus/sonnet/haiku.
# Claude 4.6+ dateless IDs are fixed model versions, not moving aliases.
CLAUDE_MODELS='
claude-haiku-5-5|cheap,fast,reasoning|verified-classification|Current Haiku; toolkit tested low/high effort; official ID checked 2026-10-09
claude-haiku-4-5-20251001|cheap,fast,legacy|verified-run|Older Haiku; $1 input / $5 output per MTok (2026-10-02 observation)
claude-sonnet-5-5|balanced,fast,coding|documented|Current Sonnet; $2 / $10 per MTok
claude-opus-5-5|frontier,coding,reasoning|documented|Current Opus; $4 / $20 per MTok
claude-fable-5-1|frontier,reasoning|listed-local|Current Fable; $10 / $50 per MTok; extra usage rules apply
claude-fable-5|frontier,reasoning,legacy|documented|Previous Fable generation
claude-opus-5|frontier,coding,legacy|documented|Previous Opus generation
claude-opus-4-8|frontier,coding,legacy|documented|Still active
claude-opus-4-7|frontier,coding,legacy|documented|Still active
claude-opus-4-6|frontier,coding,legacy|documented|Still active
claude-opus-4-5-20251101|frontier,coding,legacy|documented|Still active dated snapshot
claude-sonnet-5|balanced,coding,legacy|documented|Still active
claude-sonnet-4-6|balanced,coding,legacy|documented|Still active
claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929|balanced,coding,deprecated|documented|Retires 2026-11-30
claude-mythos-5-1|frontier,specialized,restricted|documented|Provider-listed restricted model; account access NOT established
claude-mythos-5|frontier,specialized,restricted,legacy|documented|Provider-listed restricted model; account access NOT established
claude-mythos-preview|specialized,restricted,deprecated|documented|Retirement date TBA; account access NOT established
'

# CODEX — user-visible entries in the local catalog, rechecked 2026-10-09.
# Source: ~/.codex/models_cache.json; codex-cli 0.160.0.
# https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models
# https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6-luna
# Luna 6 ($0.10 / $0.50 per MTok) is cheaper than Luna 5.6 ($0.20 / $1.20).
CODEX_MODELS='
gpt-6-luna|cheap,fast|listed-local|Current economical model
gpt-6.1-sol|balanced,coding|listed-local|Current general workhorse
gpt-6-astra|frontier,reasoning,coding|listed-local|Highest-capability general model
gpt-6-sol|balanced,coding,legacy|listed-local|Previous Sol release
gpt-5.6-luna|cheap,fast,legacy|listed-local|More expensive unit rates than GPT-6 Luna
gpt-5.6-terra|balanced,coding,legacy|listed-local|Previous comparison default
gpt-5.6-sol|frontier,coding,legacy|listed-local|Older flagship
gpt-daybreak-blue-latest|specialized,security,auto|listed-local|Moving specialized alias; outside functional QA scope
'

# GROK BUILD — authenticated catalog rechecked 2026-10-09.
# `grok models` now lists ONLY grok-4.7 (default) and the custom direct-API alias.
# Select the authenticated native model; this is NOT a cheapest-API-price claim.
# The direct alias still requires a separate XAI_API_KEY.
# https://docs.x.ai/developers/pricing
# Provider-only API IDs below need a direct-API config alias before this launcher
# can reliably select them; changing MODEL_GROK alone does not create that route.
GROK_MODELS='
grok-4-3-direct|cheap,legacy|configured-no-key|Local alias -> grok-4.3 at api.x.ai; $1.25 / $2.50 per MTok
grok-4.6|frontier,coding,legacy|provider-only|No longer listed by the authenticated CLI
grok-4.5|frontier,coding,legacy|provider-only|No longer listed by the authenticated CLI
grok-build-0.1|cheap,coding|provider-only|Lowest published text rates here: $1 / $2 per MTok; route not configured
grok-4.7|frontier,coding|verified-classification|Authenticated catalog default; toolkit single-document check passed
grok-4.20-multi-agent-0309|specialized,legacy|provider-only|Multi-agent API model; not a normal single-agent comparison
grok-4.20-0309-reasoning|reasoning,legacy|provider-only|Not configured locally
grok-4.20-0309-non-reasoning|legacy|provider-only|Not configured locally
'

# KIMI CODE — these FOUR IDs were returned by authenticated Moonshot /v1/models.
# Selectors retain the provider/ prefix required by the installed CLI.
# https://platform.kimi.ai/docs/pricing/chat (table also in chat.md)
# https://moonshotai.github.io/kimi-code/en/configuration/providers.html
# K2.6 and K2.7 Code tie at $0.95 input / $4 output per MTok; cached input
# is $0.16 vs $0.19. Actual task cost still depends on token usage.
KIMI_MODELS='
moonshotai/kimi-k2.6|cheap,vision,legacy|listed-api|Lowest cached-input price among currently listed models
moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code|cheap,balanced,coding,vision|listed-api|Same uncached rates as K2.6; coding-focused
moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code-highspeed|fast,coding,vision|listed-api|Higher throughput at $1.90 input / $8 output per MTok
moonshotai/kimi-k3|frontier,reasoning,vision|verified-classification|Configured CLI alias -> kimi-k3; toolkit tested low effort; not a browser test
'

# DEEPSEEK / REASONIX — `reasonix doctor --json` confirms both provider aliases
# and stored credentials. Select the alias, not its raw API model ID.
# Toolkit Pro: 10/10 valid answers, only 4/10 successful process exits.
# Flash compatibility run returned exit 1. Preserve failures when launching.
# https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing/
# DeepSeek now serves legacy v4-flash / v4-flash-vision-exp requests with V4.1
# Flash. The local provider still uses those legacy names: this is NOT a fixed
# V4 snapshot. Updating models.env does not rewrite ~/.reasonix/config.toml.
DEEPSEEK_MODELS='
deepseek-flash|cheap,fast,vision|configured|Alias -> legacy v4-flash IDs -> current V4.1 Flash; peak $0.30 / $1.20 per MTok
deepseek-pro|frontier,reasoning|configured|Alias -> deepseek-v4-pro (V4-Pro-0813); no vision; peak $1.32 / $3.96
'

# ANTIGRAVITY — exact selectors from `agy models`, rechecked 2026-10-09.
